// Hocket (Section 7.4): two players share one line; each player's live key
// asks the other's server for the next step, so the notes alternate A, B, A,
// B. The interval factor sees every note of the line. The players may be on
// different instruments: here the line passes between marimba and vibraphone
// note by note (as with players sharing an amadinda, use one timbre twice).
score Hocket
import std
pitches   { r, scale major C4 .. C5 }
durations { q = 1/4, e = 1/8 }
timbres   { marimba = gm(12) on 1, vibes = gm(11) on 2 }
factor line   = table step { -2..2: 1, _: 0 }
factor low    = [!carry(C5) && !carry(B4)]          // player A leaves the top to B
factor high   = [!carry(C4) && !carry(D4)]          // player B leaves the bottom to A
factor even   = machine dur uniform
play Hocket(marimba, line * low * even, vibes, line * high * even, E4, q, "H")
